# Privacy & security

**Reject** designs that send terminal command text, file contents, or raw source to remote servers by default.

- No secrets in git (API keys, tokens, `.env`, private keys)
- No raw terminal-history persistence; no raw source-code collection
- Network use must be explicit, optional, and user-configured (e.g. Giphy key)
- Webviews: validate messages, CSP, avoid unsafe HTML concatenation of untrusted data
- Invoke `orbital-privacy-reviewer` when touching terminal/editor/FS/storage/network/webview/keys/MCP
